dxil-spirv (vkd3d-proton subproject): sampler feedback on two 32-bit planes

WriteSamplerFeedback* recorded each access as a 64-bit image atomicOr into an
R64_UINT feedback map (4 bits per mip, the top 4 bits for the encoded MinMip),
which needs VK_EXT_shader_image_atomic_int64.  Metal has no 64-bit texture
atomicOr and MoltenVK reports shaderImageInt64Atomics = 0, so the AnyOS D3D12
driver could never report Sampler Feedback.  Every write touches exactly one
mip, so the 64-bit word splits into two 32-bit planes without changing what is
recorded: logical feedback texel (x, y) is stored as R32_UINT texels (2x, y) for
mips 0-7 and (2x + 1, y) for mips 8-14 plus the encoded MinMip; the write ORs
`bits << 4 * (mip & 7)` into texel 2x + (mip >> 3).  The map is twice as wide,
so the encoded mip region width moves to bits 1..4 of the image width.  vkd3d
0201 lays the map out to match.

The coalescing helper (subgroup OR per texel, one atomic per unique texel)
took the feedback image as a pointer parameter.  SPIRV-Cross deduces MSL
storage image access by starting every storage image as NonWritable +
NonReadable and loosening only images it traces atomics/writes to; it does not
follow a function parameter back to the global, so the descriptor heap was
declared read-only and Metal rejected the call ("no matching function for call
to WriteFeedback").  The helper now references the global resource variable
itself (plus the descriptor index for arrays and heaps, also part of the
coalescing key so lanes naming different maps are not merged), one helper per
variable.  The upstream R64 helper is left unused.

No 64-bit image atomic is emitted or tracked for feedback, so the
VKD3D_SHADER_META_FLAG_USES_INT64_ATOMICS_IMAGE PSO gate no longer applies.

